    "category": "architecture",
    "title": "Multi-stage Docker build with pre-installed CLI dependencies for portable AI tooling",
    "body": "The project adopts a multi-stage Docker strategy to bundle a Rust binary with external CLI tools (Claude and GitHub CLIs) into a single lightweight image. This ensures the 'diwa' tool has all necessary dependencies for insight extraction and repository interaction out-of-the-box, reducing setup friction for users who do not have these tools installed locally. The approach separates compilation from runtime, keeping the final image small by using a minimal Ubuntu base.",
    "files": [
      "Dockerfile"
    ],
    "tags": "docker, ci-cd, dependency-management, rust, ai-tools"
  },
  {
    "commit_sha": "a83172980736906c4e0fcac7bf7903e13cf50bf7903e13cf50bf6",
    "category": "pattern",
    "title": "Hybrid FTS5 + vector search for semantic insight extraction from terse commits",
    "body": "The system demonstrates that combining full-text search (FTS5) with vector embeddings allows users to find insights using natural language queries even when the exact keywords are not present in the commit messages. By using an LLM to extract structured 'insights' (decisions, patterns) from raw git history, the tool transforms noisy, terse developer notes into a searchable knowledge base that captures the 'why' behind changes.",
    "files": [
      "README.md"
    ],
    "tags": "search, vector-db, fts5, llm, knowledge-management, semantic-search"
  },
  {
    "commit_sha": "a83172980736906c4e0fcac7bf7903e13cf50bf6",
    "category": "decision",
    "title": "Provisioning multiple installation paths (Homebrew, script, Docker) for developer accessibility",
    "body": "To maximize adoption and accommodate different developer environments, the project provides three distinct installation methods: a Homebrew tap for macOS users, a curl-based install script with fallbacks for Linux/Windows, and a Docker image for containerized workflows. This redundancy ensures that developers can easily integrate the tool into their existing CI/CD pipelines or local development setups without significant configuration overhead.",
    "files": [
      "install.sh",
      "README.md"
    ],
    "tags": "distribution, installation, developer-experience, homebrew, docker"
  }
]

